# Attach contract — LLVM is the reference backend

File: oodac/docs/silent-miscompile-prevention.oot

LLVM IR is the reference ISA. `oodac check` is the front door of `oodac build`. A check-fail source must not ship an ELF.

A new `--backend` is allowed only as a second consumer of the typed artifact (tokens + type env + cap set + source coords) that check writes. That backend lives in `emit/<name>/`. It imports `types/` and the artifact. It does not import another backend's lowering.

`--backend llvm` is the product arm: `emit/llvm/` consumes the typed artifact and clang links oodar. Residual names (c, wasm, x86) exit 2.

LLVM lowering must fail closed rather than emit a lying ELF. The unique bar is the hostile probe a new backend must also pass: cap-sealed, List/Option/Result kinds, landlock, std-import, tokenize-once artifact mutate, four product mains.

Status: LLVM is the reference. Attach is open. Residual backends are not product.
